# Line endings, decided here rather than by whatever each machine has
# core.autocrlf set to. Without this the repository's contents depend on who
# committed them: CI runs on Linux, development happens on Windows, and the same
# file arrives with different bytes from each.
#
# LF in the repository for everything text. Odin, JavaScript, CSS and Markdown
# are all indifferent to which they get on disk.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell is the exception. Some versions choke on LF in a script with a
# here-string, and tools/install-vst3.ps1 has one.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touched. A byte changed in any of these is a corrupt file, not a
# reformatted one -- and .sy1 patches are a binary format that merely looks
# textual in places.
*.dll binary
*.wasm binary
*.wav binary
*.sy1 binary
*.fxb binary
